* EE577A Spring 2026 - 512-bit SRAM Array Functional Test Vector File
* USC ID: 9924884571
*
* Write Order (last digit=1, so start from seq 1):
*   seq1 -> seq2 -> seq3 -> seq4 -> seq5 -> seq6 -> seq7 -> seq8 -> seq9 -> seq0
*
* Read Order (digits of USC ID: 9-9-2-4-8-8-4-5-7-1):
*   seq9 -> seq9 -> seq2 -> seq4 -> seq8 -> seq8 -> seq4 -> seq5 -> seq7 -> seq1
*
* !! IMPORTANT NOTE !!
*    seq1 (addr=01010) and seq3 (addr=01010) share the SAME address.
*    seq3 is written AFTER seq1 and will overwrite it.
*    When reading seq1 (addr=01010), the expected output is 4C36 (from seq3), NOT 984C.
*
* Address/Data Table (from Figure 4):
*   seq | A[4:0] | A_bar[4:0] | data (hex) | data (bin)
*   ----+--------+------------+------------+--------------------
*    0  | 01011  |   10100    |    143B    | 0001 0100 0011 1011
*    1  | 01010  |   10101    |    984C    | 1001 1000 0100 1100
*    2  | 10110  |   01001    |    211B    | 0010 0001 0001 1011
*    3  | 01010  |   10101    |    4C36    | 0100 1100 0011 0110  <- SAME ADDR AS SEQ1
*    4  | 10011  |   01100    |    E15C    | 1110 0001 0101 1100
*    5  | 11111  |   00000    |    5F2B    | 0101 1111 0010 1011
*    6  | 10100  |   01011    |    9054    | 1001 0000 0101 0100
*    7  | 00111  |   11000    |    FF83    | 1111 1111 1000 0011
*    8  | 10001  |   01110    |    19D7    | 0001 1001 1101 0111
*    9  | 11011  |   00100    |    1A2B    | 0001 1010 0010 1011
*
* Clock period = 4ns (50% duty cycle, 2ns high / 2ns low)
* You may replace the 'clk' column with a vpulse in your testbench.
* trise/tfall = 5ps (0.005ns)
*
* Signal timing within each 4ns WRITE cycle (base time = T):
*   T+0.0 : CLK↑  | pre_en=1, pre_en_SA=1 | addr & data registered by DFF
*   T+0.5 : pre=0 | decoder_en=1, write_en=1 | WL opens, data driven onto BL
*   T+2.0 : CLK↓
*   T+2.5 : decoder_en=0, write_en=0 | WL closes (after BL discharges ~80mV)
*   T+3.0 : pre_en=1 | BL/BLB recharge for next cycle
*
* Signal timing within each 4ns READ cycle (base time = T):
*   T+0.0 : CLK↑  | pre_en=1, pre_en_SA=1 | addr registered
*   T+0.5 : pre=0 | pre_en_SA=0 | decoder_en=1 | read_en=0 | WL opens, SA connected
*   T+1.5 : sense_en=1  <- BL-BLB differential >= 80mV at this point
*   T+2.0 : CLK↓
*   T+2.5 : decoder_en=0, sense_en=0 | WL closes, SA disabled
*   T+3.0 : pre_en=1, pre_en_SA=1, read_en=1 | recharge
*
* NOTE on read_en polarity: read_en=0 enables PMOS M5/M6 in sense amp (active LOW).
*   If your M5/M6 are NMOS (active HIGH), invert the read_en column.
*==============================================================================

